1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,776
September, nineteen seventy-three.

2
00:00:01,836 --> 00:00:04,770
Two engineers at Ford finish an eight-page report
and send it

3
00:00:04,770 --> 00:00:08,645
to the federal government. On page six there
is a table.

4
00:00:08,705 --> 00:00:11,221
It counts deaths, and it prices them.

5
00:00:11,281 --> 00:00:14,541
Four years from now a magazine will reprint
that table,

6
00:00:14,601 --> 00:00:17,651
and the country will decide it knows what Ford
did.

7
00:00:17,711 --> 00:00:22,098
Almost nobody will notice what the table is about.

8
00:00:22,158 --> 00:00:25,184
Two of those eight pages describe a car rolling
over.

9
00:00:25,244 --> 00:00:26,643
One more thing before we start,

10
00:00:26,644 --> 00:00:30,035
because it changes how everything after it
should be heard.

11
00:00:30,095 --> 00:00:33,857
Most of what is known about this case comes
from a single appellate opinion,

12
00:00:33,875 --> 00:00:36,750
and that opinion says of itself that it viewed
the evidence

13
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:40,923
in the light most favourable to the side
that had already won.

14
00:00:40,983 --> 00:00:46,413
It is not a neutral account. It was never trying
to be.

15
00:00:46,473 --> 00:00:50,057
In nineteen sixty-eight Ford began designing a new
subcompact.

16
00:00:50,117 --> 00:00:55,233
A vice president named Lee Iacocca conceived
the project and was its moving force.

17
00:00:55,293 --> 00:00:58,472
The objective was a car at or below two thousand
pounds,

18
00:00:58,473 --> 00:01:01,756
to sell for no more than two thousand dollars.

19
00:01:01,816 --> 00:01:04,935
The court that later heard the case put the next
part plainly.

20
00:01:04,995 --> 00:01:07,155
The Pinto was a rush project,

21
00:01:07,215 --> 00:01:11,314
so that styling preceded engineering and dictated
engineering design

22
00:01:11,315 --> 00:01:13,362
to a greater degree than usual.

23
00:01:13,422 --> 00:01:17,398
Among the engineering decisions dictated
by styling was the placement

24
00:01:17,398 --> 00:01:20,835
of the fuel tank. The tank went behind the rear
axle.

25
00:01:20,895 --> 00:01:24,061
There was a reason, and it was not a sinister one.

26
00:01:24,121 --> 00:01:27,281
A law professor who read the trial record put it
this way:

27
00:01:27,341 --> 00:01:30,761
if the fuel tank were located above the axle,

28
00:01:30,821 --> 00:01:33,742
the Pinto would have been left with a very small
trunk.

29
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:39,497
That location was not unusual. It
was a commonplace at the time in American cars.

30
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:42,444
What was unusual was what was left behind it.

31
00:01:42,504 --> 00:01:46,463
Between the back of the tank and the rear
of the car there were nine or ten inches

32
00:01:46,464 --> 00:01:51,357
of what engineers call crush space. The opinion
says nine or ten.

33
00:01:51,417 --> 00:01:53,375
Schwartz says nine.

34
00:01:53,435 --> 00:01:56,514
Either way it is less than any other American
automobile,

35
00:01:56,515 --> 00:02:00,037
and less than any Ford subcompact built overseas.

36
00:02:00,097 --> 00:02:03,634
The bumper, in Schwartz's words, was essentially
ornamental.

37
00:02:03,694 --> 00:02:07,231
And here is the kind of sentence this film keeps
having to say.

38
00:02:07,291 --> 00:02:10,778
At the criminal trial eight years later a witness
called

39
00:02:10,778 --> 00:02:13,070
by the prosecution was asked about that bumper,

40
00:02:13,071 --> 00:02:16,401
and said it was about the same as the ones
on the Gremlin,

41
00:02:16,401 --> 00:02:20,649
the Vega and the Dodge Colt. I would say they
were all bad.

42
00:02:20,709 --> 00:02:22,528
Ford crash-tested the car.

43
00:02:22,588 --> 00:02:26,306
The tests were run against a fuel-system standard
the federal government

44
00:02:26,306 --> 00:02:28,633
had proposed but not yet imposed.

45
00:02:28,693 --> 00:02:31,952
The results are in the record, and they
are not ambiguous.

46
00:02:32,012 --> 00:02:34,871
The crash tests revealed that the Pinto's fuel
system

47
00:02:34,872 --> 00:02:39,138
as designed could not meet
the twenty-mile-per-hour proposed standard.

48
00:02:39,139 --> 00:02:43,466
At twenty-one miles an hour, prototypes
had the tank driven forward and punctured.

49
00:02:43,526 --> 00:02:45,705
A production car struck at the same speed

50
00:02:45,706 --> 00:02:49,846
into a fixed barrier had the filler neck torn away
from the tank,

51
00:02:49,906 --> 00:02:55,490
and the tank itself punctured by a bolt head
on the differential housing. Bolts.

52
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:58,459
On the housing. Facing the tank.

53
00:02:58,519 --> 00:03:01,638
The federal regulator says the same thing
in its own file.

54
00:03:01,698 --> 00:03:05,357
Its investigation report of nineteen seventy-eight
records

55
00:03:05,358 --> 00:03:09,057
that the Pinto performed badly in these initial
crash tests,

56
00:03:09,058 --> 00:03:13,558
and that Ford responded by somewhat modifying
the Pinto's rear design

57
00:03:13,558 --> 00:03:18,864
before production began. The fixes had prices,
and the opinion lists them.

58
00:03:18,924 --> 00:03:22,275
A smooth differential housing, two dollars ten.

59
00:03:22,335 --> 00:03:25,919
A shock-absorbent flak suit around the tank, four
dollars.

60
00:03:25,979 --> 00:03:29,343
A nylon bladder, between five twenty-five
and eight dollars.

61
00:03:29,344 --> 00:03:35,086
Eight more inches of crush space, six dollars
forty. And one combined figure.

62
00:03:35,146 --> 00:03:38,497
Another number is going to try to take its place.

63
00:03:38,557 --> 00:03:43,237
Equipping the car with a reinforced rear
structure, a smooth axle,

64
00:03:43,297 --> 00:03:46,317
an improved bumper and additional crush space,

65
00:03:46,377 --> 00:03:49,996
at a total cost of fifteen dollars and thirty
cents,

66
00:03:49,997 --> 00:03:53,896
would have made the fuel tank safe in a rear-end
collision at thirty-four

67
00:03:53,897 --> 00:03:57,791
to thirty-eight miles an hour, by a vehicle
the size of a Ford Galaxie.

68
00:03:57,851 --> 00:04:00,667
Fifteen thirty. Hold on to it.

69
00:04:00,727 --> 00:04:03,893
The results of those tests did not stay
with the engineers.

70
00:04:03,953 --> 00:04:07,699
The court found that the Pinto crash test results
had been forwarded up the chain

71
00:04:07,699 --> 00:04:09,632
of command to the ultimate decision-makers,

72
00:04:09,633 --> 00:04:14,363
and were known to the Ford officials who decided
to go forward with production.

73
00:04:14,423 --> 00:04:19,028
In April nineteen seventy-one there was a product
review meeting.

74
00:04:19,088 --> 00:04:20,861
A report was handed round.

75
00:04:20,921 --> 00:04:24,920
The court describes it as a report prepared
by Ford engineers pertaining

76
00:04:24,921 --> 00:04:29,700
to the financial impact of a proposed federal
standard on fuel system integrity,

77
00:04:29,701 --> 00:04:34,582
and the cost savings which would accrue
from deferring even minimal fixes.

78
00:04:34,642 --> 00:04:39,036
This document is not the famous one. This one
was in evidence.

79
00:04:39,096 --> 00:04:41,295
It is quoted in the opinion's own footnotes,

80
00:04:41,296 --> 00:04:45,939
under the heading Fuel System integrity Program
financial review,

81
00:04:45,939 --> 00:04:48,252
and it recommends a delay.

82
00:04:48,312 --> 00:04:50,792
Its recommendation, in its own words:

83
00:04:50,852 --> 00:04:55,391
a design cost savings of ten point nine million
dollars,

84
00:04:55,392 --> 00:04:59,431
for nineteen seventy-four and seventy-five,
can be realised by this delay.

85
00:04:59,432 --> 00:05:01,530
Two more lines from the same paper.

86
00:05:01,590 --> 00:05:05,777
Currently there are no plans for forward models
to repackage the fuel tanks.

87
00:05:05,837 --> 00:05:10,860
And, of the Pinto: smallest car line with most
difficulty in achieving compliance.

88
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:14,843
In October of that year Ford officials decided
against incorporating any

89
00:05:14,843 --> 00:05:17,569
of the modifications into current Pintos.

90
00:05:17,629 --> 00:05:21,770
The company would wait until the federal regulator
clarified its position.

91
00:05:21,830 --> 00:05:25,089
The regulator clarified it in nineteen
seventy-three.

92
00:05:25,149 --> 00:05:26,748
It issued the fuel-tank standard,

93
00:05:26,749 --> 00:05:32,030
and ruled that the standard would apply only
to nineteen seventy-seven models.

94
00:05:32,090 --> 00:05:35,223
Four model years away.

95
00:05:35,283 --> 00:05:38,463
On the twenty-eighth of May, nineteen seventy-two,

96
00:05:38,523 --> 00:05:43,418
Mrs Lilly Gray set out in her Pinto from Anaheim
for Barstow, to meet her husband.

97
00:05:43,478 --> 00:05:47,758
The car was six months old and had been driven
approximately three thousand miles.

98
00:05:47,818 --> 00:05:52,538
A thirteen-year-old neighbour was in the passenger
seat. She changed lanes.

99
00:05:52,598 --> 00:05:56,566
Then the car stalled and coasted to a halt
in the middle lane of the freeway.

100
00:05:56,567 --> 00:05:58,850
The reason was not the fuel tank.

101
00:05:58,910 --> 00:06:03,469
It was later established that the carburettor
float had become so saturated

102
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:06,430
with gasoline that it suddenly sank,

103
00:06:06,490 --> 00:06:10,388
opening the float chamber and causing the engine
to flood and stall.

104
00:06:10,448 --> 00:06:12,128
A car came up behind her.

105
00:06:12,188 --> 00:06:16,627
How fast it was going is the single most contested
fact in this entire story,

106
00:06:16,628 --> 00:06:21,784
and both answers are in the record. The jury took
the plaintiffs' version.

107
00:06:21,844 --> 00:06:25,264
The Galaxie had been travelling from fifty
to fifty-five miles per hour,

108
00:06:25,324 --> 00:06:28,463
but before the impact had been braked to a speed
of from twenty-eight

109
00:06:28,464 --> 00:06:32,974
to thirty-seven miles per hour. Ford's position
at trial was the opposite.

110
00:06:33,032 --> 00:06:34,541
Schwartz, who read the record,

111
00:06:34,541 --> 00:06:38,292
notes that the appellate opinion does not mention
it at any point:

112
00:06:38,352 --> 00:06:41,871
Ford's basic position was that the approaching car
had not slowed down at all,

113
00:06:41,872 --> 00:06:46,043
and had struck the Gray car at a speed in excess
of fifty miles per hour.

114
00:06:46,103 --> 00:06:52,057
A nineteen seventy-two Ford Pinto hatchback
automobile unexpectedly stalled

115
00:06:52,057 --> 00:06:52,942
on a freeway,

116
00:06:52,943 --> 00:06:55,716
erupting into flames when it was rear ended
by a car proceeding

117
00:06:55,716 --> 00:06:56,990
in the same direction.

118
00:06:56,991 --> 00:07:02,386
Mrs Gray died a few days later of congestive heart
failure as a result of the burns.

119
00:07:02,446 --> 00:07:03,940
The boy survived.

120
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,719
He survived only through heroic medical measures,

121
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:10,556
and he underwent numerous and extensive surgeries
and skin grafts.

122
00:07:10,616 --> 00:07:12,342
And then the court stops.

123
00:07:12,402 --> 00:07:16,842
Because Ford does not contest the amount
of compensatory damages awarded, it wrote,

124
00:07:16,902 --> 00:07:20,667
no purpose would be served by further description
of the injuries suffered

125
00:07:20,667 --> 00:07:25,554
by Grimshaw. That is a court with every reason
to describe those injuries declining

126
00:07:25,554 --> 00:07:29,889
to describe them. He was thirteen. He is a private
person.

127
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:34,669
This film stops where the opinion stopped, and it
will not go past it,

128
00:07:34,729 --> 00:07:40,056
and you have now been told why. Other defendants
settled before and during trial.

129
00:07:40,116 --> 00:07:45,393
The case went to verdict only against Ford Motor
Company. The trial ran six months.

130
00:07:45,453 --> 00:07:47,829
The jury deliberated for eight hours.

131
00:07:47,889 --> 00:07:53,089
It awarded the boy two million eight hundred

132
00:07:53,149 --> 00:07:55,898
and forty-one thousand dollars in compensatory
damages,

133
00:07:55,898 --> 00:07:59,116
and one hundred and twenty-five million dollars
in punitive damages.

134
00:07:59,116 --> 00:08:01,735
It awarded Mrs Gray's family six hundred
and fifty-nine thousand,

135
00:08:01,735 --> 00:08:03,188
six hundred and eighty.

136
00:08:03,188 --> 00:08:05,551
By stipulation, sums the plaintiffs had already
received

137
00:08:05,552 --> 00:08:07,791
from the other defendants were deducted,

138
00:08:07,792 --> 00:08:11,881
and the judgment was entered at two million five
hundred and sixteen thousand,

139
00:08:11,881 --> 00:08:15,371
and five hundred and fifty-nine thousand six
hundred and eighty.

140
00:08:15,371 --> 00:08:17,538
Then Ford moved for a new trial,

141
00:08:17,598 --> 00:08:21,258
and the judge did the thing that is missing
from almost every retelling.

142
00:08:21,318 --> 00:08:24,437
He granted the motion unless the boy gave
the money back.

143
00:08:24,497 --> 00:08:26,737
On Ford's motion for a new trial,

144
00:08:26,797 --> 00:08:31,319
Grimshaw was required to remit all but three
and a half million dollars

145
00:08:31,319 --> 00:08:34,688
of the punitive award, as a condition of denial
of the motion.

146
00:08:34,689 --> 00:08:37,901
One hundred and twenty-five million, down to three
and a half.

147
00:08:37,961 --> 00:08:40,987
A reduction of ninety-seven point two per cent.

148
00:08:41,047 --> 00:08:43,126
The judge's stated reasons are worth hearing,

149
00:08:43,127 --> 00:08:46,210
because they are not what you would expect.

150
00:08:46,270 --> 00:08:51,349
He noted that Ford's net worth was seven point
seven billion dollars,

151
00:08:51,350 --> 00:08:54,113
and that its profits during the last quarter
of the year

152
00:08:54,113 --> 00:08:57,620
in the financial statement introduced
into evidence were more

153
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,945
than twice the punitive award.

154
00:08:58,945 --> 00:09:02,170
On that basis the award was not disproportionate
to Ford's net assets,

155
00:09:02,171 --> 00:09:07,172
or to its profit generating capacity. He reduced
it anyway.

156
00:09:07,232 --> 00:09:10,412
His stated reason was proportion of a different
kind:

157
00:09:10,472 --> 00:09:14,810
the amount of the punitive award was forty-four
times the compensatory award.

158
00:09:14,870 --> 00:09:18,361
And he added something that ought to be quoted
more often than it is.

159
00:09:18,421 --> 00:09:22,340
He was not suggesting, he said, that the amount
was warranted,

160
00:09:22,341 --> 00:09:28,460
or that the jury did utilise Exhibit one
twenty-five, or any other exhibits,

161
00:09:28,461 --> 00:09:31,862
and if they did, that they were justified
in so doing.

162
00:09:31,863 --> 00:09:36,017
Nobody knows how that jury reached one hundred
and twenty-five million dollars.

163
00:09:36,018 --> 00:09:38,859
The judge who watched the whole trial refused
to guess.

164
00:09:38,919 --> 00:09:42,085
Mrs Gray's family received nothing punitive
at all.

165
00:09:42,145 --> 00:09:44,885
Under California law as it then stood,

166
00:09:44,945 --> 00:09:48,504
punitive damages were not recoverable
in a wrongful death action,

167
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:51,162
and the motion to add them was denied.

168
00:09:51,222 --> 00:09:54,202
The woman who died recovered nothing punitive.

169
00:09:54,262 --> 00:09:57,103
The boy who lived recovered three and a half
million.

170
00:09:57,163 --> 00:10:00,409
The Court of Appeal affirmed all of it
on the twenty-ninth of May,

171
00:10:00,409 --> 00:10:04,018
nineteen eighty-one. A rehearing was denied
in June.

172
00:10:04,078 --> 00:10:08,080
The California Supreme Court denied review
on the tenth of September.

173
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:11,830
The appellate court changed no number.

174
00:10:11,890 --> 00:10:14,289
In September nineteen seventy-seven,

175
00:10:14,290 --> 00:10:17,550
four years after that eight-page report was posted
to Washington,

176
00:10:17,610 --> 00:10:21,511
a magazine called Mother Jones published
an article by Mark Dowie.

177
00:10:21,571 --> 00:10:23,808
It was titled Pinto Madness.

178
00:10:23,868 --> 00:10:27,359
The magazine held a press conference in Washington
to launch it.

179
00:10:27,419 --> 00:10:32,371
Dowie was accompanied by Ralph Nader. The article
makes a number of claims.

180
00:10:32,431 --> 00:10:35,086
One of them became the thing everybody knows.

181
00:10:35,146 --> 00:10:37,726
By conservative estimates, Dowie wrote,

182
00:10:37,786 --> 00:10:41,645
Pinto crashes have caused five hundred burn deaths
to people

183
00:10:41,646 --> 00:10:46,160
who would not have been seriously injured
if the car had not burst into flames.

184
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:48,748
The figure could be as high as nine hundred.

185
00:10:48,749 --> 00:10:51,543
The article gives no source for either number.

186
00:10:51,603 --> 00:10:54,258
Not a footnote, not an agency, not a study.

187
00:10:54,318 --> 00:10:58,691
Two figures, in one sentence, and nothing behind
them in the text.

188
00:10:58,751 --> 00:11:01,870
Then the sentence that became the whole popular
story.

189
00:11:01,930 --> 00:11:06,630
Ford waited eight years, Dowie wrote,
because its internal cost-benefit analysis,

190
00:11:06,690 --> 00:11:09,430
which places a dollar value on human life,

191
00:11:09,490 --> 00:11:12,340
said it was not profitable to make the changes
sooner.

192
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:15,194
And the one that misdescribes the document.

193
00:11:15,254 --> 00:11:17,333
This cost-benefit analysis argued

194
00:11:17,334 --> 00:11:20,293
that Ford should not make an eleven-dollar-per-car
improvement

195
00:11:20,294 --> 00:11:24,098
that would prevent one hundred and eighty fiery
deaths a year.

196
00:11:24,099 --> 00:11:27,565
Hold that eleven dollars too. It comes back.

197
00:11:27,625 --> 00:11:30,244
What the article did next is almost never told,

198
00:11:30,245 --> 00:11:33,809
and it produced the only reliable numbers anybody
has.

199
00:11:33,869 --> 00:11:35,701
It moved the federal government.

200
00:11:35,702 --> 00:11:39,286
The regulator's own investigation report opens
on this point.

201
00:11:39,346 --> 00:11:43,725
Following public release of the article, Pinto
Madness, the agency initiated,

202
00:11:43,726 --> 00:11:46,785
on the eleventh of August nineteen seventy-seven,

203
00:11:46,786 --> 00:11:50,465
a preliminary evaluation of the alleged safety
defect,

204
00:11:50,466 --> 00:11:55,004
and on the thirteenth of September, a formal
defect investigation case.

205
00:11:55,064 --> 00:11:58,369
Then it lists what it did, and the list is worth
reading.

206
00:11:58,429 --> 00:12:00,928
The author of the magazine article, Mark Dowie,

207
00:12:00,929 --> 00:12:05,148
was asked to make available to the agency
the documentation and evidence upon

208
00:12:05,149 --> 00:12:09,429
which his article was based. Congressional
inquiries were processed.

209
00:12:09,432 --> 00:12:12,192
The Fatal Accident Reporting System was searched.

210
00:12:12,193 --> 00:12:15,777
Ford was requested to provide technical and legal
data.

211
00:12:15,837 --> 00:12:19,776
And a test program of staged vehicle-to-vehicle
rear-end collisions was developed,

212
00:12:19,777 --> 00:12:23,322
and a contract awarded for the performance
of these tests.

213
00:12:23,382 --> 00:12:26,269
Over nine hundred inquiries came
in from the public.

214
00:12:26,329 --> 00:12:30,763
Of all of them, one letter reported a fire
the agency had not already heard about.

215
00:12:30,809 --> 00:12:36,008
A parked Pinto, struck from behind by a nineteen
sixty-nine Pontiac Firebird,

216
00:12:36,009 --> 00:12:40,683
in a residential area. No bodily injuries
and no fatalities were sustained.

217
00:12:40,743 --> 00:12:43,584
Ford was asked for its own count, and gave it.

218
00:12:43,644 --> 00:12:46,717
Thirty-five rear-impact fuel-leakage or fire
cases.

219
00:12:46,777 --> 00:12:49,478
Twenty-nine lawsuits and liability claims.

220
00:12:49,538 --> 00:12:54,608
Twenty-six fatalities reported,
of which twenty-five were Pinto occupants.

221
00:12:54,668 --> 00:12:56,147
And a breakdown of the claims

222
00:12:56,148 --> 00:13:00,333
that is worth putting beside the phrase everyone
remembers about Ford settling

223
00:13:00,333 --> 00:13:01,177
out of court.

224
00:13:01,237 --> 00:13:06,337
Cases settled out of court or by judgement
against Ford or its co-defendants: eight.

225
00:13:06,367 --> 00:13:08,557
Cases pending trial: nineteen.

226
00:13:08,617 --> 00:13:12,897
Cases settled in favour of Ford
or under investigation: two.

227
00:13:12,957 --> 00:13:18,120
Then the agency added everything it had from every
source, and wrote one paragraph.

228
00:13:18,180 --> 00:13:22,553
It is the paragraph this whole film exists to put
back into circulation.

229
00:13:22,613 --> 00:13:24,733
In total, the agency wrote,

230
00:13:24,793 --> 00:13:28,172
the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration
is aware of thirty-

231
00:13:28,173 --> 00:13:32,452
eight cases in which rear-end collisions of Pinto
vehicles have resulted

232
00:13:32,453 --> 00:13:37,249
in fuel tank damage, fuel system leakage
and-or ensuing fire.

233
00:13:37,309 --> 00:13:41,108
These cases have resulted in a total
of twenty-seven fatalities sustained

234
00:13:41,109 --> 00:13:46,837
by Pinto occupants, of which one is reported
to have resulted from impact injuries.

235
00:13:46,897 --> 00:13:48,716
In addition, twenty-four occupants

236
00:13:48,717 --> 00:13:54,124
of these Pinto vehicles have sustained non-fatal
burn injuries. Twenty-seven.

237
00:13:54,184 --> 00:13:57,443
One of them from the impact rather than the fire.

238
00:13:57,503 --> 00:14:02,042
And because this film is about people quoting
a number without its document,

239
00:14:02,043 --> 00:14:03,653
here is the rest of the document.

240
00:14:03,654 --> 00:14:06,074
The agency set out, in its own words,

241
00:14:06,134 --> 00:14:08,910
why its data might be wrong in both directions.

242
00:14:08,970 --> 00:14:13,715
Fire or explosion is not a standard data element
on most police reporting forms.

243
00:14:13,775 --> 00:14:17,455
If a death due to burns occurred sometime
after the crash,

244
00:14:17,515 --> 00:14:21,770
it is less likely that it would be reported
on the officer's accident report.

245
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:25,790
The system does not record the cause of death,
only its fact;

246
00:14:25,850 --> 00:14:30,522
it does not distinguish between deaths due
to impact and those caused by the fire.

247
00:14:30,582 --> 00:14:32,122
That is the number.

248
00:14:32,182 --> 00:14:36,462
Twenty-seven, with the government's own reasons
for doubting it, attached.

249
00:14:36,522 --> 00:14:40,801
In May nineteen seventy-eight the agency issued
an initial determination

250
00:14:40,802 --> 00:14:43,081
that the Pinto's fuel system was defective,

251
00:14:43,082 --> 00:14:46,991
and scheduled a hearing for the fourteenth of June
to enable Ford to reply.

252
00:14:46,992 --> 00:14:52,547
The hearing never happened. On the nineteenth
of June the agency received a recall.

253
00:14:52,607 --> 00:14:58,487
Campaign seven eight V one four three. One million
four hundred thousand vehicles.

254
00:14:58,547 --> 00:15:01,886
The remedy was a longer fuel filler pipe
with an improved seal,

255
00:15:01,887 --> 00:15:06,171
and a polyethylene shield installed on the front
of the fuel tank.

256
00:15:06,231 --> 00:15:09,629
Twelve days after a jury in California returned
its verdict.

257
00:15:09,689 --> 00:15:12,344
Five days before the agency's hearing.

258
00:15:12,404 --> 00:15:17,056
And one last figure for this act,
which is the least famous number in the story.

259
00:15:17,116 --> 00:15:19,036
According to an agency official,

260
00:15:19,096 --> 00:15:23,991
only fifty-three per cent of Pinto owners
responded to the recall offer extended

261
00:15:23,991 --> 00:15:30,554
by Ford in nineteen seventy-eight. Just over half
the cars came back.

262
00:15:30,783 --> 00:15:35,621
Nobody, in fifty years of telling this story,
has read out the title of the table.

263
00:15:35,681 --> 00:15:40,726
So. The document has a name, and it is not the one
it is usually given.

264
00:15:40,786 --> 00:15:45,859
It is called Fatalities Associated with Crash
Induced Fuel Leakage and Fires, by E.

265
00:15:45,859 --> 00:15:47,583
S. Grush and C. S.

266
00:15:47,583 --> 00:15:52,466
Saunby, on the letterhead of Ford's Environmental
and Safety Engineering office,

267
00:15:52,526 --> 00:15:56,186
and it is headed Attachment Two. Attachment
to what?

268
00:15:56,246 --> 00:15:59,845
To a submission Ford filed with the federal
regulator on the nineteenth

269
00:15:59,846 --> 00:16:03,085
of September, nineteen seventy-three,

270
00:16:03,086 --> 00:16:05,405
captioned a Petition for Reconsideration

271
00:16:05,406 --> 00:16:08,991
of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard Number
Three Oh One.

272
00:16:08,992 --> 00:16:12,830
It is not an internal memorandum. It is a filing.

273
00:16:12,890 --> 00:16:15,070
It says so in its first paragraph:

274
00:16:15,130 --> 00:16:18,963
the agency has issued Notice Two of Docket seventy
dash twenty,

275
00:16:18,963 --> 00:16:22,529
and Notice One of Docket seventy-three dash
twenty,

276
00:16:22,530 --> 00:16:27,687
both regarding fuel system integrity. And on page
four it says what it is analysing.

277
00:16:27,747 --> 00:16:31,606
The analysis discussed below concerns the static
rollover requirement proposed

278
00:16:31,607 --> 00:16:37,597
for the standard. Rollover. Not rear impact.

279
00:16:37,657 --> 00:16:39,290
A car turning over.

280
00:16:39,350 --> 00:16:44,110
The paper contradicts itself on which standard
number that requirement belongs to —

281
00:16:44,170 --> 00:16:50,349
page four says three oh one and the table caption
says two oh eight —

282
00:16:50,350 --> 00:16:53,999
and rather than quietly pick one, this film tells
you the paper does that.

283
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,380
Schwartz, who went and found the filing, states it
in one sentence:

284
00:16:57,440 --> 00:17:01,779
it was the rollover situation,
and not the rear-end-impact situation,

285
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:07,636
that was the subject of the Ford document. Now
the table itself, one line at a time.

286
00:17:07,696 --> 00:17:12,676
Savings: one hundred and eighty burn deaths,

287
00:17:12,736 --> 00:17:15,281
one hundred and eighty serious burn injuries,

288
00:17:15,281 --> 00:17:17,671
two thousand one hundred burned vehicles.

289
00:17:17,671 --> 00:17:21,650
Unit cost: two hundred thousand dollars per death,
sixty-seven thousand per injury,

290
00:17:21,651 --> 00:17:25,267
seven hundred per vehicle. Total benefit,
forty-nine and a half million dollars.

291
00:17:25,268 --> 00:17:27,527
And then the line that makes it a different
document

292
00:17:27,528 --> 00:17:32,682
from the one everybody thinks they are quoting.
Sales: eleven million cars.

293
00:17:32,742 --> 00:17:37,926
One and a half million light trucks. Eleven
million cars is not a Ford model line.

294
00:17:37,986 --> 00:17:42,520
It is the American market for a year. The paper
says so itself.

295
00:17:42,580 --> 00:17:46,259
The retail price equivalent of the vehicle
modifications necessary

296
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:49,299
to assure compliance with the static rollover
portion

297
00:17:49,300 --> 00:17:52,939
of the proposed standard has been determined
by Ford to be an average

298
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:57,588
of eleven dollars per passenger car and eleven
dollars per light truck.

299
00:17:57,648 --> 00:17:59,167
While these are Ford costs,

300
00:17:59,168 --> 00:18:02,160
they have been applied across the industry
in this analysis.

301
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:04,921
The word Pinto does not appear in that table.

302
00:18:04,981 --> 00:18:09,911
Two more things the same eight pages say, and they
cut in opposite directions.

303
00:18:09,971 --> 00:18:12,487
The first is Ford arguing its own case.

304
00:18:12,547 --> 00:18:17,867
The agency's estimate of fatalities
in fire-involved crashes, the report says,

305
00:18:17,927 --> 00:18:21,239
appears to overstate the seriousness of the fire
problem.

306
00:18:21,299 --> 00:18:24,849
The basis is a sample of twenty-four, of whom,
the paper says,

307
00:18:24,849 --> 00:18:28,969
in over half of the instances the deceased
was not burned at all.

308
00:18:29,029 --> 00:18:33,867
The second is the opposite, and it
is the strangest fact in this episode.

309
00:18:33,927 --> 00:18:34,458
On page one,

310
00:18:34,458 --> 00:18:38,486
the same report tells the government
that the likelihood of a given crash resulting

311
00:18:38,487 --> 00:18:42,227
in fuel spillage is much higher for rear impacts —

312
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:45,426
twenty-six per cent with spillage in the sample
studied —

313
00:18:45,427 --> 00:18:49,783
than for other crash types, such as frontals,
at three and a half per cent.

314
00:18:49,784 --> 00:18:53,893
The document that is quoted to prove Ford ignored
rear-impact fires is a document

315
00:18:53,893 --> 00:18:58,105
that told the federal government rear impact
was by far the worst case.

316
00:18:58,165 --> 00:19:00,832
Which leaves the two hundred thousand dollars.

317
00:19:00,833 --> 00:19:03,859
The report attributes it, twice,
to the government.

318
00:19:03,919 --> 00:19:08,676
The agency has calculated a value of two hundred
thousand dollars for each fatality.

319
00:19:08,677 --> 00:19:10,542
And it goes further than that.

320
00:19:10,602 --> 00:19:14,962
The casualty to dollars conversion factors used
in this study, it says,

321
00:19:15,022 --> 00:19:18,458
were the societal cost values prepared
by the agency.

322
00:19:18,518 --> 00:19:22,722
These values are generally higher
than similarly-defined costs from other sources,

323
00:19:22,778 --> 00:19:27,721
and their use does not signify that Ford accepts
or concurs in the values.

324
00:19:27,781 --> 00:19:30,111
And a shorter film would stop there.

325
00:19:30,171 --> 00:19:34,019
The man who established most of that changed
his mind about it, in print.

326
00:19:34,047 --> 00:19:37,746
Schwartz first concluded that Ford's use
of the figure was clearly proper,

327
00:19:37,747 --> 00:19:41,625
because it was the same datum the regulator
would be using.

328
00:19:41,685 --> 00:19:44,260
Then, in his words, he did further homework.

329
00:19:44,261 --> 00:19:47,000
Contrary to my earlier understanding, he wrote,

330
00:19:47,001 --> 00:19:51,288
in its standard-setting the agency was not,
in the early nineteen seventies,

331
00:19:51,288 --> 00:19:54,637
relying on a two hundred thousand dollar
life-value figure.

332
00:19:54,638 --> 00:19:57,678
It was taking costs and benefits into account,

333
00:19:57,738 --> 00:20:01,338
and essentially finessing the question
of the monetary value of life,

334
00:20:01,398 --> 00:20:03,617
while at the same time releasing documents

335
00:20:03,618 --> 00:20:07,974
that set forth a two hundred thousand dollar
life-value datum.

336
00:20:08,034 --> 00:20:10,550
There is more, and it is worse for Ford.

337
00:20:10,610 --> 00:20:13,855
The government's nineteen seventy-two report
had said

338
00:20:13,855 --> 00:20:18,929
that its own figure represented the minimum,
but not the maximum,

339
00:20:18,930 --> 00:20:21,958
that society should spend in preventing highway
fatalities.

340
00:20:21,958 --> 00:20:23,260
Schwartz's conclusion on that:

341
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:29,020
the nineteen seventy-three Ford report can fairly
be faulted for not taking account

342
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:32,209
of the agency's explanation of the implications
of its own figure.

343
00:20:32,209 --> 00:20:33,948
Ford's answer, also in the record,

344
00:20:33,949 --> 00:20:37,196
is that it used the government's number in part
because it was higher

345
00:20:37,196 --> 00:20:40,243
than other life-value estimates known
to the company.

346
00:20:40,303 --> 00:20:44,119
So the honest version is narrower than the popular
correction.

347
00:20:44,179 --> 00:20:47,775
The two hundred thousand dollars
is the government's published figure.

348
00:20:47,776 --> 00:20:50,247
It was not the government's decision rule.

349
00:20:50,259 --> 00:20:52,523
And Ford can fairly be faulted for using it

350
00:20:52,523 --> 00:20:55,295
without saying what the government said about it.

351
00:20:55,296 --> 00:21:00,387
One more thing, and it is small and it
is not small. Mother Jones knew.

352
00:21:00,447 --> 00:21:03,586
In a nineteen seventy-two report, Dowie wrote,

353
00:21:03,587 --> 00:21:08,459
the agency decided a human life was worth two
hundred thousand seven hundred

354
00:21:08,459 --> 00:21:09,532
and twenty-five dollars.

355
00:21:09,532 --> 00:21:13,944
That sentence is two sentences after the line
about Ford having a better idea.

356
00:21:14,004 --> 00:21:17,263
The correction was already in the article
that created the problem.

357
00:21:17,323 --> 00:21:19,699
And that report was never in evidence.

358
00:21:19,759 --> 00:21:24,012
The appellate opinion records Ford's objection
to counsel's closing argument

359
00:21:24,012 --> 00:21:28,672
in these terms: Ford argues that the documentation
referred to by Mr Copp,

360
00:21:28,672 --> 00:21:32,816
the Grush-Saunby Report, was excluded
from evidence.

361
00:21:32,876 --> 00:21:37,262
The jury that returned one hundred and twenty-five
million dollars never saw it.

362
00:21:37,263 --> 00:21:39,639
Schwartz gives the procedural history.

363
00:21:39,699 --> 00:21:43,618
The plaintiffs did not even claim
that the document was relevant to the issue

364
00:21:43,619 --> 00:21:48,279
of liability; they attempted to introduce it
on the issue of punitive damages,

365
00:21:48,339 --> 00:21:51,224
as indicative of Ford's corporate mentality.

366
00:21:51,284 --> 00:21:54,704
After considering the matter over a period
of several weeks,

367
00:21:54,764 --> 00:21:57,352
the trial judge ruled against admissibility.

368
00:21:57,389 --> 00:21:59,468
And in a footnote he gives the judge's reason,

369
00:21:59,469 --> 00:22:02,691
which is the last thing anyone would guess.

370
00:22:02,751 --> 00:22:06,750
A primary reason given by the trial judge
in ruling against the admissibility

371
00:22:06,751 --> 00:22:10,003
of the Ford report was that Ford was using
the figure

372
00:22:10,003 --> 00:22:12,233
that the agency itself preferred.

373
00:22:12,293 --> 00:22:17,152
The document was kept out because the number in it
belonged to the government. So.

374
00:22:17,212 --> 00:22:18,474
Two prices.

375
00:22:18,534 --> 00:22:20,973
Eleven dollars is a rollover-compliance figure,

376
00:22:20,974 --> 00:22:24,714
for every passenger car and light truck sold
in America,

377
00:22:24,714 --> 00:22:28,759
in a nineteen seventy-three filing that a court
excluded.

378
00:22:28,819 --> 00:22:33,970
Fifteen dollars and thirty cents is an appellate
court's figure for a package

379
00:22:33,970 --> 00:22:38,626
of rear-impact fixes on one car line,
in an opinion that stands.

380
00:22:38,686 --> 00:22:43,559
They are not the same number. They never were.

381
00:22:43,619 --> 00:22:47,958
On the tenth of August, nineteen seventy-eight,
in Elkhart County, Indiana,

382
00:22:47,959 --> 00:22:51,382
three young women died after a van struck
the Pinto they were in.

383
00:22:51,442 --> 00:22:55,722
The wire report named them: Judy Ulrich, eighteen,
of Osceola, Indiana;

384
00:22:55,782 --> 00:22:59,921
her sixteen-year-old sister Lynn; and their cousin
Donna Ulrich, eighteen,

385
00:22:59,922 --> 00:23:04,243
of Roanoke, Illinois. A grand jury indicted
the company.

386
00:23:04,303 --> 00:23:08,630
Three counts of reckless homicide, and one count
of criminal recklessness.

387
00:23:08,690 --> 00:23:12,599
The maximum penalties would total thirty-six
thousand dollars in fines.

388
00:23:12,659 --> 00:23:14,246
Thirty-six thousand.

389
00:23:14,306 --> 00:23:18,165
Against a company whose net worth the California
trial judge had put

390
00:23:18,166 --> 00:23:20,351
at seven point seven billion.

391
00:23:20,411 --> 00:23:24,041
The grand jury could have indicted individual Ford
executives.

392
00:23:24,101 --> 00:23:26,988
It chose to charge only the corporation.

393
00:23:27,048 --> 00:23:30,737
This case has two numbers, and that is a fact
about its shape.

394
00:23:30,738 --> 00:23:36,035
It was filed in Elkhart Superior Court as number
five three two four,

395
00:23:36,035 --> 00:23:39,919
on the thirteenth of September nineteen
seventy-eight —

396
00:23:39,919 --> 00:23:43,354
and the source for that is a California appellate
opinion five years later,

397
00:23:43,354 --> 00:23:46,183
surveying every corporate homicide prosecution
then known.

398
00:23:46,183 --> 00:23:49,084
The venue then changed, and judgment was entered
at Winamac,

399
00:23:49,085 --> 00:23:54,406
in the Pulaski County Circuit Court, as number
eleven dash four three one.

400
00:23:54,466 --> 00:23:56,378
The trial ran ten weeks.

401
00:23:56,438 --> 00:23:59,421
And here is the structural fact that explains
the whole thing,

402
00:23:59,421 --> 00:24:03,319
which almost nobody who tells this story has ever
mentioned.

403
00:24:03,379 --> 00:24:07,698
The reckless homicide statute Indiana charged
under had been enacted only

404
00:24:07,699 --> 00:24:09,470
in nineteen seventy-seven.

405
00:24:09,530 --> 00:24:14,321
So Ford could not be prosecuted for the reckless
design of the Pinto.

406
00:24:14,381 --> 00:24:19,741
The prosecution needed to show a reckless failure,
after nineteen seventy-seven,

407
00:24:19,801 --> 00:24:24,416
to repair or to warn. The design was not on trial.
It could not be.

408
00:24:24,476 --> 00:24:28,536
And largely because of the narrowness
of the resulting issue,

409
00:24:28,596 --> 00:24:32,795
the prosecution was not able to secure
the admission of the internal Ford documents

410
00:24:32,796 --> 00:24:38,251
on which it had hoped to build its case. What
was left was a fight about speed.

411
00:24:38,311 --> 00:24:41,575
The defence showed films of test crashes
in which other cars struck

412
00:24:41,575 --> 00:24:45,238
by the same model of van sustained similar damage.

413
00:24:45,298 --> 00:24:47,798
The prosecutor described the resources:

414
00:24:47,858 --> 00:24:50,623
it has just been a matter of David and Goliath.

415
00:24:50,660 --> 00:24:55,358
On the thirteenth of March nineteen eighty,
the jury found Ford not guilty.

416
00:24:55,418 --> 00:24:57,657
The Indiana Law Review, surveying the year,

417
00:24:57,658 --> 00:24:59,943
recorded what the jurors said afterwards.

418
00:24:59,944 --> 00:25:03,087
Interviews with the jury after trial indicated
that the issue

419
00:25:03,087 --> 00:25:06,175
of closing speed was never resolved by the jury.

420
00:25:06,235 --> 00:25:09,122
The case was not appealed from the trial level.

421
00:25:09,182 --> 00:25:13,002
That is why there is no Indiana appellate opinion
about any of this,

422
00:25:13,062 --> 00:25:16,676
and why almost everything written about that trial
since has come

423
00:25:16,676 --> 00:25:22,168
from two newspapers and a book. So the popular
story is wrong in five places.

424
00:25:22,228 --> 00:25:26,994
The document is about rollover. The units
are the whole industry.

425
00:25:27,054 --> 00:25:31,634
The price of a life belonged to the government.
The jury never saw the paper.

426
00:25:31,694 --> 00:25:34,442
And the criminal case ended in an acquittal.

427
00:25:34,502 --> 00:25:36,421
None of which makes the car innocent,

428
00:25:36,422 --> 00:25:40,268
and the man who established most of it says
so on the same pages.

429
00:25:40,328 --> 00:25:43,588
In the government's crash-testing, Schwartz
writes,

430
00:25:43,648 --> 00:25:46,368
the Pinto was compared to the Chevrolet Vega,

431
00:25:46,428 --> 00:25:51,399
often regarded as having the least safe gas tank
of the other subcompacts for sale

432
00:25:51,399 --> 00:25:53,264
in America. In this process,

433
00:25:53,324 --> 00:25:56,889
the Pinto consistently flunked tests that the Vega
was able to pass.

434
00:25:56,949 --> 00:25:58,228
At the criminal trial,

435
00:25:58,229 --> 00:26:02,615
Ford put in exhibits showing that Pintos were one
point nine per cent of the cars

436
00:26:02,615 --> 00:26:07,168
on American roads and were involved in one point
nine per cent

437
00:26:07,169 --> 00:26:08,868
of fatal accidents accompanied by fire.

438
00:26:08,868 --> 00:26:11,746
The prosecution's own expert confirmed Ford's
data.

439
00:26:11,806 --> 00:26:15,840
Then the same expert narrowed it to the accidents
that were actually the subject

440
00:26:15,840 --> 00:26:19,105
of the case: rear-end fire fatalities.

441
00:26:19,165 --> 00:26:20,824
These data showed that Pintos,

442
00:26:20,825 --> 00:26:24,984
while comprising one point nine per cent
of the auto population,

443
00:26:24,985 --> 00:26:28,883
were responsible for four point one per cent
of all such fatalities.

444
00:26:28,883 --> 00:26:32,312
One point nine of the cars. Four point one
of the deaths.

445
00:26:32,372 --> 00:26:35,770
And then the fact this film has been walking
towards.

446
00:26:35,830 --> 00:26:38,392
Ford had its own comparative memorandum.

447
00:26:38,452 --> 00:26:42,091
It showed the Pinto's rear-fire fatality rate
below the Gremlin's,

448
00:26:42,092 --> 00:26:48,212
and considerably above the respective rates
of the Vega, Toyota, Mazda and Datsun.

449
00:26:48,272 --> 00:26:51,131
Schwartz's next clause: perhaps for this reason,

450
00:26:51,132 --> 00:26:55,014
Ford did not introduce the memorandum during
the criminal trial.

451
00:26:55,074 --> 00:26:58,093
The company that was acquitted had a document
that would have hurt it,

452
00:26:58,094 --> 00:27:03,370
and did not put it in. And the professor who took
the myth apart ends up here.

453
00:27:03,430 --> 00:27:09,210
There was a package of changes — a stronger
bumper, a smooth bolt-free differential,

454
00:27:09,270 --> 00:27:13,887
hat sections and cross-members —
that would have improved the Pinto's safety.

455
